WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:35.451
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:00:41.813 --> 00:00:46.068
THE DREAM LIFE OF MR. KIM

00:00:47.152 --> 00:00:50.238
Five, six, seven, eight.

00:00:50.322 --> 00:00:52.366
One, two, three.

00:00:56.161 --> 00:00:58.205
Do the safety exercises properly!

00:01:04.336 --> 00:01:05.837
Stop fooling around.

00:01:12.219 --> 00:01:13.387
Back to your positions.

00:01:14.429 --> 00:01:17.349
We'll go by my count, no music,
starting with number eight.

00:01:18.141 --> 00:01:20.811
-He's freaking scary.
-Begin.

00:01:22.145 --> 00:01:24.106
You got zapped at karaoke last night.

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:25.065
Oh, that?

00:01:26.525 --> 00:01:28.944
Who's laughing? Answer me!

00:01:30.654 --> 00:01:31.530
Your names.

00:01:33.865 --> 00:01:34.950
Your names!

00:01:35.742 --> 00:01:37.494
-Lee Dal-jae.
-And the one next to him.

00:01:37.577 --> 00:01:39.538
-Choi Mi-ra.
-What was that?

00:01:40.414 --> 00:01:41.915
-Choi Mi-ra!
-Choi Mi-ra.

00:01:41.998 --> 00:01:44.376
One warning each
for safety rule violations.

00:01:44.459 --> 00:01:45.585
What?

00:01:45.669 --> 00:01:47.254
-This is ridiculous. I--
-Quiet.

00:01:47.796 --> 00:01:49.506
Again. Back to your positions.

00:01:53.301 --> 00:01:55.137
We're starting again from number eight.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.596
Begin.

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:05.772
Safety slogan, ready!

00:02:07.733 --> 00:02:08.692
Start!

00:02:08.775 --> 00:02:11.319
-Helmets!
-Helmet, check! Uniform, check!

00:02:11.403 --> 00:02:12.279
Safety shoes, check!

00:02:12.362 --> 00:02:14.239
-Safety, safety, safety!
-Safety, safety, safety!

00:02:14.322 --> 00:02:16.742
Again, with discipline! Start!

00:02:16.825 --> 00:02:17.868
Helmet, check!

00:02:17.951 --> 00:02:19.953
Uniform, check! Safety shoes, check!

00:02:20.036 --> 00:02:22.456
-Safety, safety, safety!
-Safety, safety, safety!

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.292
Less doubt…

00:02:25.375 --> 00:02:27.043
-More determination!
-More determination!

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:30.756
Dismissed.

00:02:31.381 --> 00:02:33.175
Move it, people. Hurry!

00:02:39.139 --> 00:02:40.223
What is this?

00:02:43.143 --> 00:02:45.771
It's a ladder. Why do you ask?

00:02:45.854 --> 00:02:48.815
A ladder with no work platform
is a safety rule violation.

00:02:48.899 --> 00:02:52.611
I don't use it for work.
I use it as a chair.

00:02:56.198 --> 00:02:59.493
Then get a proper chair to sit on.

00:03:00.619 --> 00:03:01.703
I'll put it away.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.583
Why won't this thing fold?

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:08.418
It's stiff.

00:03:12.964 --> 00:03:13.840
Your chin strap.

00:03:14.883 --> 00:03:15.759
Excuse me?

00:03:15.842 --> 00:03:17.302
I said, fasten your chin strap.

00:03:21.598 --> 00:03:24.684
Why is your helmet so small?
Don't you have any that fit?

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.686
What's all this right here?

00:03:27.229 --> 00:03:28.313
Tidy it up.

00:03:29.105 --> 00:03:31.858
No one cleans up around here.

00:03:32.526 --> 00:03:33.485
What the heck?

00:03:35.695 --> 00:03:36.947
What are you doing?

00:03:39.115 --> 00:03:39.991
Ms. Lee.

00:03:41.076 --> 00:03:42.118
I asked what you're doing.

00:03:43.495 --> 00:03:45.121
Something's wrong, so I'm checking it out.

00:03:45.205 --> 00:03:46.456
What's wrong?

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:49.251
The load ratio's higher than usual,
and there's a bearing problem.

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:50.460
Is that urgent?

00:03:52.546 --> 00:03:53.421
Yes.

00:03:54.089 --> 00:03:56.216
I was walking very slowly,

00:03:56.299 --> 00:03:58.718
and I almost tripped
and fell over all this.

00:03:58.802 --> 00:04:00.846
When everyone rushes out to grab lunch,

00:04:00.929 --> 00:04:02.347
it's going to be dangerous.

00:04:03.723 --> 00:04:05.475
Yes, I understand,

00:04:05.559 --> 00:04:07.352
but I need to do this now.

00:04:07.435 --> 00:04:09.771
Who said you couldn't?

00:04:11.189 --> 00:04:13.108
I said to clean up!

00:04:20.574 --> 00:04:22.742
I'll be back in an hour
to check this again.

00:04:22.826 --> 00:04:24.578
And that's not an empty threat.

00:04:25.704 --> 00:04:26.830
You and your excuses.

00:04:36.214 --> 00:04:38.133
What's with that guy this morning?

00:04:38.216 --> 00:04:40.385
Did he fight with his wife or something?

00:04:40.468 --> 00:04:41.970
Take it out. We'll fix this later.

00:04:42.053 --> 00:04:43.013
Let's get that.

00:04:55.317 --> 00:04:56.443
What's this?

00:04:56.526 --> 00:04:58.695
-It's about voluntary retirement.
-What?

00:04:58.778 --> 00:05:00.363
The application period is one month.

00:05:00.447 --> 00:05:01.865
Think it over and let us know.

00:05:01.948 --> 00:05:02.949
BULLETIN BOARD

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:04.117
What is this?

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.036
Was this announced today?

00:05:06.578 --> 00:05:09.748
They want us to post it here too.
As if anyone here would apply.

00:05:11.541 --> 00:05:13.460
VOLUNTARY RETIREMENT APPLICATIONS

00:05:13.543 --> 00:05:15.128
What? All of a sudden?

00:05:15.211 --> 00:05:17.422
-What is it?
-I haven't heard anything.

00:05:19.132 --> 00:05:22.427
EPISODE 7
CAUGHT IN THE DOWNPOUR

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:23.762
VOLUNTARY RETIREMENT APPLICATION

00:05:23.845 --> 00:05:27.057
-The company must be in real trouble.
-Song-hee, we should start coming early.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:29.351
We can't draw attention
to ourselves in times like these.

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:30.352
Be invisible.

00:05:30.435 --> 00:05:32.145
Be invisible.

00:05:34.314 --> 00:05:36.316
-Sung-gu.
-Jeez! What is it?

00:05:36.399 --> 00:05:37.817
-Gosh.
-What? Why?

00:05:37.901 --> 00:05:40.612
I've been hearing whispers
about Mr. Kim coming back.

00:05:40.695 --> 00:05:41.613
What?

00:05:41.696 --> 00:05:43.406
Damn you.

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:44.908
Don't say stuff like that right now.

00:05:44.991 --> 00:05:48.161
Mr. Do is already
looking at me differently as it is.

00:05:48.244 --> 00:05:49.245
Why do you say that?

00:05:49.329 --> 00:05:51.289
He's supposed to pick 20 people

00:05:51.373 --> 00:05:53.291
from the factory for a layoff list.

00:05:53.375 --> 00:05:55.710
Wait. The factory is offering
voluntary retirement too?

00:05:55.794 --> 00:05:57.879
Why would Mr. Kim make that list?

00:05:57.963 --> 00:05:59.714
Apparently, that's what the job entails.

00:05:59.798 --> 00:06:01.549
Would writing up that list

00:06:01.633 --> 00:06:03.468
bring him back to HQ?

00:06:05.095 --> 00:06:06.805
There's a precedent.

00:06:06.888 --> 00:06:08.974
So that's what that was about.

00:06:09.057 --> 00:06:11.810
Mr. Kim asked me to look up
that one executive.

00:06:11.893 --> 00:06:12.978
Which executive?

00:06:13.812 --> 00:06:15.188
Who was it? There was someone.

00:06:15.271 --> 00:06:18.733
He became an executive
right after coming back from the factory.

00:06:20.235 --> 00:06:22.028
This must be a real headache.

00:06:22.112 --> 00:06:25.824
Good luck staying off the list.

00:06:27.784 --> 00:06:29.577
-Go on. Get lost.
-Later.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.498
GENERAL MANAGER KIM NAK-SU

00:06:33.581 --> 00:06:34.708
LEE DAL-JAE, PERSONAL DETAILS

00:06:34.791 --> 00:06:35.959
EVALUATION
SAFETY VIOLATION: -1

00:06:36.042 --> 00:06:37.168
TOTAL SCORE: -1

00:06:37.252 --> 00:06:39.212
EVALUATION
SAFETY VIOLATION: 0

00:06:39.295 --> 00:06:40.839
SAFETY VIOLATION: -1

00:06:40.922 --> 00:06:42.007
CHOI MI-RA, PERSONAL DETAILS

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:44.342
Choi Mi-ra. Deduction…

00:06:45.385 --> 00:06:47.178
LEE JU-YOUNG
FACTORY SUPERVISOR

00:06:47.262 --> 00:06:48.680
FATHER: DECEASED, MOTHER: DECEASED

00:06:49.597 --> 00:06:50.682
Lee Ju-young.

00:06:51.182 --> 00:06:53.810
Just keep a low profile

00:06:54.602 --> 00:06:57.480
and leave whenever you want.
That's all you have to do.

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:03.903
For the first time since coming here,
I feel like I'm doing real work.

00:07:06.698 --> 00:07:08.867
LEE SANG-MIN
SAFETY VIOLATION: -1

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:10.744
UNMARRIED, FATHER: ALIVE, MOTHER: ALIVE

00:07:13.872 --> 00:07:14.998
Shoot, I'm late.

00:07:15.081 --> 00:07:19.085
RECEPTION, PAYMENT

00:07:22.422 --> 00:07:23.673
Enjoy your meal.

00:07:25.383 --> 00:07:26.468
Mr. Kim.

00:07:26.551 --> 00:07:28.136
-Come this way.
-For what?

00:07:28.219 --> 00:07:30.263
You should go ahead and eat first.

00:07:30.346 --> 00:07:31.473
No, it's fine.

00:07:31.556 --> 00:07:33.224
We insist. You must be very busy.

00:07:33.308 --> 00:07:34.893
-Mr. Kim, move to the front.
-What?

00:07:34.976 --> 00:07:36.102
Are they serious?

00:07:36.186 --> 00:07:37.812
-Go ahead.
-We'll eat after you.

00:07:38.438 --> 00:07:41.107
-What was the point of coming early?
-Unbelievable.

00:07:41.691 --> 00:07:42.901
Pile it on.

00:07:44.611 --> 00:07:46.154
Gosh.

00:07:46.237 --> 00:07:48.823
That's… Okay, that's enough.

00:07:48.907 --> 00:07:50.366
Thank you so much.

00:08:01.169 --> 00:08:04.255
RICE KEEPS US GOING!
SAFETY KEEPS US WORKING!

00:08:04.339 --> 00:08:05.799
We always have extras.

00:08:19.896 --> 00:08:21.856
Attention, all employees.

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.943
Thank you for your hard work today.

00:08:25.443 --> 00:08:27.362
Have a safe trip home.

00:08:28.822 --> 00:08:30.323
-See ya.
-You too.

00:08:30.406 --> 00:08:32.659
-I'm heading out.
-Wait. Let's go together.

00:08:33.368 --> 00:08:34.828
-Have a good one.
-You too.

00:08:34.911 --> 00:08:36.538
-See you tomorrow.
-You too.

00:08:36.621 --> 00:08:38.915
-Take care.
-You too.

00:08:38.998 --> 00:08:40.500
-Good night, Mr. Kim.
-You too, Mr. Kim.

00:08:40.583 --> 00:08:42.168
-You too.
-One second, Mr. Kim.

00:08:44.754 --> 00:08:45.797
We need to talk.

00:08:46.923 --> 00:08:47.799
About what?

00:08:49.342 --> 00:08:50.343
You go on ahead.

00:08:55.014 --> 00:08:55.890
What is it?

00:08:55.974 --> 00:08:58.601
A notice for voluntary retirement
was suddenly put up.

00:08:58.685 --> 00:09:00.145
Have you heard anything?

00:09:00.228 --> 00:09:02.897
Heard what?
That was also my first time seeing it.

00:09:03.731 --> 00:09:05.275
It's just a little strange.

00:09:06.317 --> 00:09:08.361
No one here would ever apply
for voluntary retirement.

00:09:08.444 --> 00:09:09.612
HQ knows that very well.

00:09:09.696 --> 00:09:12.115
Then ask headquarters yourself.
Why ask me?

00:09:12.824 --> 00:09:14.200
You don't usually give a damn.

00:09:14.284 --> 00:09:15.785
I could say the same thing to you.

00:09:15.869 --> 00:09:18.204
You've never given a damn
about the factory.

00:09:18.288 --> 00:09:19.497
What's with the sudden change?

00:09:19.581 --> 00:09:21.207
I'm just doing my job.

00:09:21.291 --> 00:09:23.918
You said you guys take the hit
when non-experts are in charge.

00:09:24.002 --> 00:09:25.837
I'm trying to do things right.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:26.796
Is that a problem?

00:09:28.506 --> 00:09:29.507
Are we done here?

00:09:30.842 --> 00:09:31.843
I'm leaving.

00:09:35.346 --> 00:09:36.598
Are you hiding something?

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:41.728
Are you HQ's errand boy?

00:09:43.521 --> 00:09:44.439
I figured

00:09:45.148 --> 00:09:46.608
something was going on.

00:09:49.277 --> 00:09:50.695
Don't cross the line.

00:10:11.299 --> 00:10:14.177
-Hey, son.
-Dad, are you off work?

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.178
Yes. Why?

00:10:16.012 --> 00:10:18.431
Have you had dinner yet?

00:10:18.514 --> 00:10:20.433
No, I haven't. Why do you ask?

00:10:20.975 --> 00:10:24.437
I was wondering
if we could have dinner together.

00:10:25.104 --> 00:10:27.482
I'd like that, but I'm in Asan.

00:10:27.982 --> 00:10:30.401
Yes, I'm nearby too.

00:10:32.779 --> 00:10:33.988
There he is, Han-na.

00:10:34.072 --> 00:10:34.948
What?

00:10:36.366 --> 00:10:38.034
EMPLOYEE DORMITORY

00:10:43.248 --> 00:10:45.625
-Dad.
-Oh, hey. Hi--

00:10:45.708 --> 00:10:47.085
Hello, Mr. Kim.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:48.878
Hello.

00:10:50.213 --> 00:10:51.923
-Go ahead and park.
-Okay.

00:10:58.263 --> 00:10:59.973
-Come on in.
-Thank you.

00:11:00.056 --> 00:11:01.599
Oh my.

00:11:02.892 --> 00:11:04.060
Goodness.

00:11:04.727 --> 00:11:05.770
Come in.

00:11:08.314 --> 00:11:09.482
Gosh.

00:11:15.321 --> 00:11:18.616
So what did you want to explain to me?

00:11:19.242 --> 00:11:20.702
Next.

00:11:23.454 --> 00:11:25.415
Even with short consumption cycles,

00:11:25.498 --> 00:11:28.459
our loyal customer base,
with its strong brand loyalty,

00:11:28.543 --> 00:11:31.713
would gladly open their wallets

00:11:31.796 --> 00:11:34.507
even if we were to make
fire extinguishers or gas masks.

00:11:35.425 --> 00:11:36.384
-Okay.
-Next.

00:11:36.467 --> 00:11:37.510
PROFIT IS INCALCULABLE

00:11:37.593 --> 00:11:40.513
That's it.
Thank you for listening, Mr. Kim.

00:11:41.764 --> 00:11:43.391
All right. Thank you.

00:11:44.017 --> 00:11:47.353
So you're explaining this to me because…

00:11:47.979 --> 00:11:48.980
Su-gyeom has become

00:11:49.063 --> 00:11:52.984
the CEO of our company,
Jealousy, My Strength.

00:11:53.067 --> 00:11:55.737
That company you mentioned a while back

00:11:56.362 --> 00:11:58.323
-about destruction?
-Yes, that one.

00:11:58.865 --> 00:11:59.741
That's what happened.

00:11:59.824 --> 00:12:02.201
Gosh. So you're the CEO there now.

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:06.581
-Congratulations.
-Mr. Kim. We have the ideas.

00:12:06.664 --> 00:12:09.375
And ACT has the infrastructure.

00:12:09.459 --> 00:12:12.086
What if we formed a strategic alliance?

00:12:12.754 --> 00:12:13.880
An "alliance"?

00:12:13.963 --> 00:12:15.214
Or you could invest.

00:12:16.215 --> 00:12:17.133
"Invest"?

00:12:19.218 --> 00:12:21.471
You should explain now as the CEO.

00:12:23.264 --> 00:12:26.017
-Well, we--
-Wait a minute.

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:29.562
Ms. Han-na, could I speak
with Su-gyeom alone?

00:12:31.147 --> 00:12:32.398
Yes.

00:12:37.862 --> 00:12:40.698
We'll be right back. Let's go.

00:12:47.497 --> 00:12:49.290
Thirty million won?

00:12:49.374 --> 00:12:50.625
I'm sorry.

00:12:50.708 --> 00:12:52.960
-Does your mother know?
-No, she doesn't.

00:12:53.044 --> 00:12:54.253
Did you gamble?

00:12:54.754 --> 00:12:55.755
No.

00:12:55.838 --> 00:12:57.590
Then were you scammed or something?

00:12:58.674 --> 00:13:01.386
Tell me the truth.
Did someone scam you or what?

00:13:08.976 --> 00:13:10.436
When do you need it by?

00:13:11.771 --> 00:13:13.648
Whenever it's convenient for you.

00:13:14.899 --> 00:13:15.775
Anytime.

00:13:15.858 --> 00:13:18.778
Are you sure it's 30 million?
Will that be enough?

00:13:19.821 --> 00:13:20.696
Yes.

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:22.949
All right. I will figure something out.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.286
Don't say a word to your mother, okay?

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:29.414
It'll just complicate things.

00:13:29.497 --> 00:13:31.332
Thanks, Dad. Thank you.

00:13:36.462 --> 00:13:38.589
What's going on between you
and that woman?

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:40.216
Don't look.

00:13:43.761 --> 00:13:45.304
I don't really know.

00:13:46.013 --> 00:13:47.140
What do you mean?

00:13:50.435 --> 00:13:53.771
At least get her some food
before you take her home.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.606
Here.

00:13:56.315 --> 00:13:57.692
-Dad.
-Take it.

00:14:10.746 --> 00:14:12.874
-Thank you, sir.
-Of course.

00:14:12.957 --> 00:14:14.250
We'll get going, Dad.

00:14:14.333 --> 00:14:15.626
Call me when you get home.

00:14:52.497 --> 00:14:56.250
Now that we have our seed money,

00:14:56.334 --> 00:14:58.169
what should we do first?

00:14:58.252 --> 00:14:59.462
I don't know.

00:15:00.296 --> 00:15:02.715
Maybe we should get new nameplates made.

00:15:04.217 --> 00:15:05.343
Just kidding.

00:15:05.968 --> 00:15:07.220
Wasn't it funny?

00:15:07.303 --> 00:15:10.223
Also, the office is too big
for just the two of us.

00:15:11.224 --> 00:15:13.976
-Don't you think?
-I'm putting it on the market.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:17.104
Until we decide on a product,
we can work at school.

00:15:17.188 --> 00:15:18.689
Okay. Let's do that.

00:15:18.773 --> 00:15:19.899
Han-na.

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.568
We have to do this right this time.

00:15:22.652 --> 00:15:24.737
And stop talking about
things like nameplates.

00:15:25.446 --> 00:15:26.489
Okay.

00:15:27.865 --> 00:15:28.950
I'm really going to try--

00:15:29.033 --> 00:15:31.077
I'm saying this
because I'm seriously worried.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:34.372
My dad made a difficult decision
to give us that money.

00:15:35.206 --> 00:15:37.750
But you're starting to sound
just like Lee Jeong-hwan.

00:15:40.878 --> 00:15:43.798
Are you comparing me
to that damn con artist?

00:15:43.881 --> 00:15:44.924
No.

00:15:45.675 --> 00:15:47.718
-I wasn't comparing.
-Then what was it?

00:15:47.802 --> 00:15:50.304
Why bring him up all of a sudden?

00:15:53.641 --> 00:15:56.060
-What is it?
-You kissed him!

00:16:31.637 --> 00:16:32.513
HEAD OF HR

00:16:32.597 --> 00:16:33.889
It's difficult, isn't it?

00:16:33.973 --> 00:16:35.349
It's not easy.

00:16:35.433 --> 00:16:37.852
That's right. It's not a simple task.

00:16:37.935 --> 00:16:41.188
To suspend or dismiss someone
for safety violations,

00:16:41.272 --> 00:16:42.648
the violations need to be repeated,

00:16:42.732 --> 00:16:45.943
or there must be a major one.

00:16:46.027 --> 00:16:47.737
You're right.

00:16:53.826 --> 00:16:54.702
Sir.

00:16:54.785 --> 00:16:57.788
Do you happen to have
a box of tissues in your office?

00:16:59.457 --> 00:17:01.208
Yes, I do.

00:17:01.292 --> 00:17:03.753
Okay. Could you pull out

00:17:03.836 --> 00:17:05.630
all the tissues from the box?

00:17:05.713 --> 00:17:06.589
What?

00:17:06.672 --> 00:17:09.508
Put all the employees' names in the box,

00:17:09.592 --> 00:17:12.553
give the box a good shake,
and draw 20 names.

00:17:14.847 --> 00:17:16.349
We'll let those people go.

00:17:18.643 --> 00:17:20.394
What kind of nonsense is this?

00:17:20.478 --> 00:17:22.897
Right. It makes no sense.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.483
But if you don't help us,

00:17:26.025 --> 00:17:27.485
we might have to go with that.

00:17:28.361 --> 00:17:29.612
Gosh.

00:17:30.196 --> 00:17:31.906
This feels so wrong.

00:17:31.989 --> 00:17:34.408
We did put out
a voluntary retirement notice, right?

00:17:34.492 --> 00:17:37.119
But they wouldn't even
look at it, would they?

00:17:37.203 --> 00:17:38.204
That's what I'm saying.

00:17:38.287 --> 00:17:40.748
The atmosphere
here at headquarters is the same.

00:17:41.248 --> 00:17:42.458
This is really killing me.

00:17:42.541 --> 00:17:44.585
GENERAL MANAGER KIM NAK-SU

00:17:46.379 --> 00:17:49.840
Sir, let's get the factory
back to normal quickly

00:17:49.924 --> 00:17:52.927
and help them come up
with a Plan B for their lives.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.387
If we don't do this right,

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:57.932
we'll have another unfortunate incident
like with Manager Heo Tae-hwan.

00:17:58.641 --> 00:18:01.143
I'm asking for your help
because it's a difficult job.

00:18:01.227 --> 00:18:04.105
And since it's difficult,
I'll make sure you're well compensated.

00:18:05.022 --> 00:18:06.691
Please help me.

00:18:10.236 --> 00:18:11.404
Keep your promise.

00:18:11.487 --> 00:18:13.739
Of course. You have three days left.

00:18:15.366 --> 00:18:16.784
I'll be waiting for your call, sir.

00:18:39.223 --> 00:18:41.434
Mr. Kim. Thanks for everything you do.

00:18:41.517 --> 00:18:44.812
-Hi.
-Please take a look over here.

00:18:44.895 --> 00:18:47.815
That's right. I completely organized
all the nipple dies.

00:18:47.898 --> 00:18:49.108
-Looks neat, right?
-It does.

00:18:49.191 --> 00:18:52.945
They might all look similar,
but they have different uses.

00:18:53.028 --> 00:18:54.947
But as for me,

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:57.408
I can tell at a glance
where everything goes.

00:18:57.491 --> 00:18:59.827
The reason I can tell them all apart is

00:19:00.327 --> 00:19:02.163
because I am a certified electrician.

00:19:02.788 --> 00:19:04.582
What's with the sudden intro?

00:19:04.665 --> 00:19:07.001
No reason. I just wanted to let you know.

00:19:07.626 --> 00:19:08.961
Mr. Kim.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.338
Keep up the good work.

00:19:12.673 --> 00:19:14.341
Thank you.

00:19:15.718 --> 00:19:16.969
Chin strap.

00:19:17.052 --> 00:19:18.679
Just carry on as usual.

00:19:18.763 --> 00:19:21.474
Carry on, everyone.

00:19:26.937 --> 00:19:28.355
Clean this area up.

00:19:28.981 --> 00:19:30.149
Get rid of this.

00:19:33.152 --> 00:19:34.403
Why is this missing?

00:19:34.487 --> 00:19:36.238
I need your name.

00:19:36.322 --> 00:19:37.865
-I'm sorry.
-Your name!

00:19:37.948 --> 00:19:39.116
One-point deduction.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:40.826
I can't get a reading.

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:42.870
Yeah, it's not showing anything, right?

00:19:43.621 --> 00:19:45.289
-Yes.
-Is it the bearing?

00:19:49.835 --> 00:19:50.920
Let's do this.

00:19:59.804 --> 00:20:00.679
What?

00:20:00.763 --> 00:20:02.807
That's a perfect split!

00:20:11.273 --> 00:20:12.274
Congratulations!

00:20:13.025 --> 00:20:15.236
-Congratulations, sir!
-Congratulations!

00:20:21.408 --> 00:20:24.203
Let's just clap.
We don't want to get on his bad side.

00:20:25.371 --> 00:20:27.081
Congratulations!

00:20:40.928 --> 00:20:42.304
So then…

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:47.899
2025 INDIVIDUAL EVALUATION FORM

00:20:56.235 --> 00:20:58.946
ACT CHICKEN GRAND OPENING
WE FRY AT 5G SPEEDS

00:20:59.029 --> 00:21:03.117
Sooner or later,
reality will hit you hard.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:05.703
Give me a call once it does.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:16.714
JINPYEONG BRANCH
23 JINPYEONG-RO, ASAN-SI, CHUNGNAM

00:21:16.797 --> 00:21:18.841
Are you interested in taking over?

00:21:18.924 --> 00:21:21.010
-Come on.
-Excuse me?

00:21:21.093 --> 00:21:23.304
You'd be great at running a chicken place.

00:21:23.387 --> 00:21:25.139
I can leave all the equipment as is.

00:21:25.222 --> 00:21:29.059
Plus, the fridge is already stocked
with the sauce I make.

00:21:29.852 --> 00:21:31.896
That's not why I came here. I--

00:21:31.979 --> 00:21:34.815
You could sell
sweet and crispy chicken or something.

00:21:35.441 --> 00:21:38.485
I don't really have
the knack for that sort of thing.

00:21:40.237 --> 00:21:42.656
I came to ask you a few questions

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:44.408
about how things work at the factory.

00:21:44.491 --> 00:21:47.119
What would a guy
who only cleaned up dog poop know?

00:21:47.953 --> 00:21:50.039
I don't know anything. Nope.

00:21:51.999 --> 00:21:53.876
Sorry to bother you.

00:21:53.959 --> 00:21:55.419
I'll just be going, then.

00:21:55.502 --> 00:21:57.421
Wait. Come on.

00:21:57.504 --> 00:21:59.381
-Not so fast.
-Excuse me?

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:03.093
Just buy a chicken, will you?

00:22:04.053 --> 00:22:05.220
If you do,

00:22:05.304 --> 00:22:07.306
then, who knows, I might be able

00:22:07.389 --> 00:22:10.809
to give you some tips
on the inner workings of the factory.

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:15.439
Okay. Please make one quickly
so it's nice and crispy.

00:22:15.522 --> 00:22:17.775
-Is regular fried chicken okay?
-Yes.

00:22:17.858 --> 00:22:19.151
You do know something, right?

00:22:19.234 --> 00:22:20.110
-Of course.
-Okay.

00:22:22.905 --> 00:22:25.908
-Chicken!
-Yes! This is going to be so good!

00:22:26.492 --> 00:22:28.118
I call dibs on this chair!

00:22:28.202 --> 00:22:29.828
I told you not to run.

00:22:31.288 --> 00:22:32.206
Hello.

00:22:32.289 --> 00:22:34.416
Hello there. Two as usual?

00:22:35.751 --> 00:22:36.752
Just one for today.

00:22:36.835 --> 00:22:39.004
Just one today?

00:22:39.088 --> 00:22:41.173
The kids always eat so well.
Isn't that right?

00:22:41.256 --> 00:22:43.801
We ate something before coming here.

00:22:43.884 --> 00:22:44.885
What?

00:22:44.969 --> 00:22:46.512
No, we didn't.

00:22:49.348 --> 00:22:51.225
We'll just have one today.

00:22:51.308 --> 00:22:53.268
All right. Have a seat.

00:22:54.395 --> 00:22:55.354
My only regulars.

00:22:56.021 --> 00:22:57.272
Please wait a moment.

00:22:59.483 --> 00:23:01.026
-Hello.
-Hey, honey.

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:03.362
-Mom, hurry!
-Sit over here.

00:23:03.445 --> 00:23:04.863
All right, I'm coming.

00:23:04.947 --> 00:23:06.865
You didn't get the kids any soda, right?

00:23:06.949 --> 00:23:08.367
-No.
-Don't get them any.

00:23:13.288 --> 00:23:14.456
Hello.

00:23:16.458 --> 00:23:19.086
-Do you know him?
-Yes, he's my team leader at work.

00:23:20.462 --> 00:23:21.797
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:23.215
I'm her husband.

00:23:23.298 --> 00:23:24.675
Hello.

00:23:25.509 --> 00:23:26.427
You should say hello.

00:23:26.510 --> 00:23:27.845
-Hello.
-Hello.

00:23:27.928 --> 00:23:30.389
Hi there, kids. Please sit down.

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:36.520
Did you order yet?

00:23:36.603 --> 00:23:38.480
-Yes.
-I see.

00:23:39.023 --> 00:23:40.607
Should we get it to go?

00:23:40.691 --> 00:23:43.110
Mi-ra's not coming home tonight.
Let's eat in my room.

00:23:43.193 --> 00:23:45.946
-Okay.
-Please don't. Enjoy your meal here.

00:23:46.030 --> 00:23:47.781
I was just about to leave anyway.

00:23:48.407 --> 00:23:51.285
Excuse me.
You haven't started my order yet, right?

00:23:51.368 --> 00:23:53.162
I'm already frying it.

00:23:53.245 --> 00:23:55.581
Oh, dear. In that case…

00:23:57.291 --> 00:24:00.169
Ms. Lee, I'm not feeling very well.

00:24:00.252 --> 00:24:02.838
Please take the chicken I ordered
and enjoy it with the kids.

00:24:02.921 --> 00:24:03.797
Pardon?

00:24:03.881 --> 00:24:05.674
No, we're fine, really.

00:24:05.758 --> 00:24:08.427
Sir, here's the money.

00:24:10.679 --> 00:24:12.848
When the chicken's ready,
please bring it to that table.

00:24:12.931 --> 00:24:15.017
Wait. We still need to talk
about my restaurant.

00:24:15.100 --> 00:24:17.144
Later. I'll come back another time.

00:24:17.227 --> 00:24:19.688
-Mr. Kim.
-Don't worry. I've already paid for it.

00:24:19.772 --> 00:24:20.689
Say thank you.

00:24:20.773 --> 00:24:22.066
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:24:22.149 --> 00:24:24.401
You're welcome. Enjoy your meal.

00:24:31.658 --> 00:24:32.951
I'll be right back.

00:24:34.078 --> 00:24:35.037
-Mr. Kim.
-Gosh.

00:24:35.120 --> 00:24:36.622
I told you I can't eat right now--

00:24:36.705 --> 00:24:38.373
You left this behind.

00:24:42.795 --> 00:24:43.754
Thank you.

00:24:44.421 --> 00:24:46.298
Gosh.

00:25:05.609 --> 00:25:06.860
You should go inside.

00:26:15.512 --> 00:26:16.586
RESUME
LEE SANG-MIN

00:26:21.476 --> 00:26:23.645
FATHER: HOSPITALIZED FOR HYPERTENSION
MOTHER: DECEASED

00:26:23.729 --> 00:26:24.938
MARRIED, TWO DAUGHTERS, ONE SON

00:26:25.022 --> 00:26:27.858
FATHER: HOSPITALIZED FOR HYPERTENSION
MOTHER: HOMEBOUND DUE TO POOR HEALTH

00:26:41.705 --> 00:26:43.624
Watch yourselves. Be careful.

00:26:44.791 --> 00:26:45.918
What's this?

00:26:46.001 --> 00:26:48.086
This isn't wrapped, is it?

00:26:48.170 --> 00:26:49.254
This needs to be wrapped.

00:26:50.464 --> 00:26:52.549
I've told you. Keep this area organized.

00:26:52.633 --> 00:26:54.426
-Yes, sir.
-One-point deduction.

00:26:55.093 --> 00:26:56.678
-But sir--
-Your name.

00:26:57.846 --> 00:26:59.139
Park Seon-myeong, Materials Team.

00:26:59.223 --> 00:27:00.641
Park--

00:27:02.559 --> 00:27:03.977
-Attention, please.
-What's going on?

00:27:04.061 --> 00:27:05.854
-A fire has broken out.
-Did something explode?

00:27:05.938 --> 00:27:07.648
Locate the fire. Go. Hurry!

00:27:09.858 --> 00:27:11.485
-Where is it?
-Fire!

00:27:11.568 --> 00:27:12.986
Where's the extinguisher?

00:27:16.990 --> 00:27:18.408
Mi-ra! Get them all out of here!

00:27:31.338 --> 00:27:32.798
Over here!

00:27:34.174 --> 00:27:35.759
Fire! Over here!

00:27:38.387 --> 00:27:39.721
Get them out of here!

00:27:46.561 --> 00:27:48.522
Get them out of here! Let's go!

00:27:48.605 --> 00:27:49.940
Get out of here! Now!

00:27:51.358 --> 00:27:53.568
Where's the fire extinguisher?
Where is it?

00:27:54.361 --> 00:27:56.530
Hit the circuit breaker! Now!

00:28:24.766 --> 00:28:25.767
Ms. Lee!

00:28:26.476 --> 00:28:27.853
Ms. Lee!

00:29:04.306 --> 00:29:05.557
Thank you.

00:29:09.436 --> 00:29:13.106
The bearings of the machine
have been causing a lot of issues lately.

00:29:13.190 --> 00:29:14.316
And also--

00:29:14.399 --> 00:29:16.193
Hold on a moment.

00:29:17.861 --> 00:29:19.363
Gosh, this is way too sweet.

00:29:19.905 --> 00:29:21.656
How did I ever drink this stuff?

00:29:25.118 --> 00:29:26.620
But then again,

00:29:26.703 --> 00:29:29.539
you folks working in the factory
need this kind of thing for energy.

00:29:29.623 --> 00:29:31.333
Isn't that right?

00:29:32.042 --> 00:29:35.170
According to the safety checklist,
there haven't been any issues for months.

00:29:35.253 --> 00:29:38.006
Circles, circles,

00:29:39.007 --> 00:29:40.217
and more circles.

00:29:42.135 --> 00:29:45.097
Those who've been
at the factory long enough

00:29:45.180 --> 00:29:46.681
can hear the sound of the engine

00:29:46.765 --> 00:29:51.353
and think,
"The machine is off rhythm today."

00:29:51.895 --> 00:29:54.856
But this isn't something
a non-expert like him can identify,

00:29:55.482 --> 00:29:58.735
since we sent him here
for our own convenience.

00:29:59.736 --> 00:30:00.695
Wouldn't you agree?

00:30:01.571 --> 00:30:03.323
Yes, that's right.

00:30:05.784 --> 00:30:08.829
I don't think it's right
to point fingers here.

00:30:08.912 --> 00:30:12.874
We should look at the overall systems
and staffing issues at the Asan factory.

00:30:12.958 --> 00:30:16.086
I believe it's time we re-evaluate them.

00:30:17.087 --> 00:30:19.464
The injured workers
have all been discharged, correct?

00:30:19.548 --> 00:30:21.216
-Yes.
-Ms. Lee.

00:30:22.050 --> 00:30:25.887
How many total workers were on the line
where the accident occurred?

00:30:26.888 --> 00:30:28.140
Twenty-one people.

00:30:28.223 --> 00:30:29.724
Okay, 21 people.

00:30:32.352 --> 00:30:36.773
In that case, could I get a list
of the workers from that line?

00:30:42.446 --> 00:30:46.700
Things just got a lot easier,
don't you think?

00:30:50.829 --> 00:30:54.624
Let's cite the workers from that line
for safety negligence

00:30:54.708 --> 00:30:57.377
and let them all go.
The numbers line up anyway.

00:30:57.461 --> 00:30:58.545
Twenty-one people.

00:31:02.716 --> 00:31:04.468
Come on.

00:31:04.551 --> 00:31:05.927
What's the problem?

00:31:06.011 --> 00:31:07.762
A safety accident occurred.

00:31:09.264 --> 00:31:11.391
Shouldn't the Safety Management
Team Leader

00:31:12.309 --> 00:31:13.602
take responsibility?

00:31:14.603 --> 00:31:15.645
Exactly.

00:31:17.856 --> 00:31:21.443
So take responsibility and step down.

00:31:22.110 --> 00:31:24.404
Come to headquarters
and bring your report.

00:31:25.697 --> 00:31:28.700
I know this wasn't easy work,

00:31:28.783 --> 00:31:30.660
but you wrapped it up nicely.

00:31:30.744 --> 00:31:33.497
You did such a great job.
I really mean it, Mr. Kim.

00:31:33.580 --> 00:31:37.292
Seriously. I'll get going now.

00:31:37.375 --> 00:31:38.877
Wait, this is…

00:31:40.420 --> 00:31:41.796
You call this "work"?

00:31:42.631 --> 00:31:46.259
I've been in sales for over 20 years,
working my tail off.

00:31:46.760 --> 00:31:48.845
And no matter how I look at it,

00:31:48.929 --> 00:31:51.848
it doesn't feel like work.

00:31:51.932 --> 00:31:53.475
If you're getting paid, it's work.

00:31:54.392 --> 00:31:55.310
Am I wrong?

00:31:55.393 --> 00:31:58.980
Did you think you were working
to make Korea an IT powerhouse?

00:31:59.064 --> 00:32:02.734
You worked to buy your wife a purse
and pay for your kid's tutors.

00:32:03.318 --> 00:32:06.988
Now that you have a good excuse,
relax and get it done.

00:32:07.072 --> 00:32:08.323
Who's going to blame you?

00:32:10.617 --> 00:32:13.203
Absolutely no one. You get it?

00:32:13.286 --> 00:32:16.873
Just give me the list.
Just the list, okay?

00:32:16.957 --> 00:32:19.000
What about the staff at headquarters?

00:32:19.709 --> 00:32:21.795
How many of them are getting the axe?

00:32:26.758 --> 00:32:27.634
At headquarters?

00:32:28.343 --> 00:32:29.761
Three.

00:32:29.844 --> 00:32:31.638
No, maybe two? Damn, I don't know.

00:32:31.721 --> 00:32:33.723
Wait, you said at least
20 from the factory,

00:32:33.807 --> 00:32:35.976
but only two from headquarters?

00:32:36.893 --> 00:32:37.769
What about it?

00:32:37.852 --> 00:32:40.397
You keep changing your story.
What the heck?

00:32:40.480 --> 00:32:44.234
What's with you? Come on, Mr. Kim.

00:32:44.317 --> 00:32:46.403
This isn't like you.

00:32:46.486 --> 00:32:49.155
You're downsizing the factory
by over 20 percent.

00:32:49.239 --> 00:32:51.533
But you're leaving the team
at headquarters untouched?

00:32:51.616 --> 00:32:54.911
What kind of restructuring is that?
Does this make any sense at all?

00:32:54.995 --> 00:32:55.870
Nak-su.

00:32:56.955 --> 00:32:59.541
What really doesn't make sense at all

00:32:59.624 --> 00:33:02.335
is for a telecom company to have
a cable factory and run it themselves.

00:33:02.419 --> 00:33:03.962
Do you get what I'm saying?

00:33:04.045 --> 00:33:04.963
What do you mean?

00:33:06.339 --> 00:33:07.632
This place will close next year.

00:33:10.176 --> 00:33:12.012
-What?
-The factory is shutting down.

00:33:12.804 --> 00:33:14.931
A major corporation
saddled with a dump like this?

00:33:15.015 --> 00:33:16.683
We're the only ones
in the world doing this.

00:33:16.766 --> 00:33:19.936
That's why we've been gradually
offering voluntary retirement.

00:33:20.020 --> 00:33:21.730
If we just shut it down suddenly,

00:33:21.813 --> 00:33:24.482
they'd raise all kinds of hell
about illegalities and lawsuits.

00:33:24.566 --> 00:33:25.859
Why not say something sooner?

00:33:25.942 --> 00:33:27.110
I am saying it now.

00:33:27.193 --> 00:33:29.904
-You should've told me from the start!
-And who do you think you are?

00:33:29.988 --> 00:33:31.031
Hey!

00:33:34.701 --> 00:33:38.580
Why should I have to explain
every little thing to you?

00:33:39.414 --> 00:33:40.415
Am I an errand boy?

00:33:40.498 --> 00:33:42.959
You've got to be kidding me.

00:33:45.378 --> 00:33:47.547
What's wrong with being an errand boy?

00:33:47.631 --> 00:33:50.550
Why are you so full of yourself?
You think you're somebody?

00:33:50.634 --> 00:33:52.469
You little bastard.

00:34:12.947 --> 00:34:14.658
The Super Giga Internet.

00:34:14.741 --> 00:34:17.202
After causing that huge mess,

00:34:17.285 --> 00:34:20.205
you should've been fired.
But they spared you.

00:34:20.288 --> 00:34:23.541
You should be on your knees
thanking the company.

00:34:23.625 --> 00:34:26.544
You might as well be the errand boy.
What else would you do?

00:34:26.628 --> 00:34:27.712
Right.

00:34:28.880 --> 00:34:30.674
They sent you here for safety management.

00:34:30.757 --> 00:34:33.510
That's why this whole mess happened.

00:34:36.888 --> 00:34:39.724
Nak-su. Let's do some work.

00:34:41.059 --> 00:34:42.686
You can leave if you don't want to.

00:34:46.314 --> 00:34:48.316
Jeez.

00:34:55.699 --> 00:34:56.825
Mr. Kim.

00:34:57.617 --> 00:35:00.829
You've got two days left.
We still have a long way to go.

00:35:00.912 --> 00:35:02.789
I'm asking for your cooperation.

00:35:30.650 --> 00:35:31.609
DO NOT CROSS THIS LINE

00:35:31.693 --> 00:35:34.612
-How many of us will get fired?
-How should I know?

00:35:35.113 --> 00:35:38.450
The accident happened on our line.
Do we have to take the blame?

00:35:38.533 --> 00:35:40.994
Why should we take the blame?

00:35:41.077 --> 00:35:42.787
Especially when
there are so many higher-ups.

00:35:42.871 --> 00:35:45.290
I told upper management
that there was a problem so many times.

00:35:45.373 --> 00:35:48.668
-I still have so many loans to pay off.
-I have so many expenses.

00:35:48.752 --> 00:35:50.503
-This is hopeless.
-I agree.

00:35:50.587 --> 00:35:52.213
Why is everyone so gloomy?

00:35:53.715 --> 00:35:57.051
Why don't we get something to eat?
You must not have had lunch yet.

00:35:57.719 --> 00:35:59.387
Let's just go eat. Okay?

00:36:01.931 --> 00:36:03.308
Let's eat!

00:36:04.684 --> 00:36:06.019
Let's eat.

00:36:08.021 --> 00:36:09.022
Let's eat.

00:36:09.105 --> 00:36:10.857
SEOKAM PORK BARBECUE

00:36:10.940 --> 00:36:13.234
Okay. Cheers!

00:36:13.735 --> 00:36:16.696
-This stone grill looks amazing.
-Right?

00:36:16.780 --> 00:36:18.323
Bon appétit!

00:36:26.581 --> 00:36:27.749
This is so juicy.

00:36:28.625 --> 00:36:29.959
Told you this place was no joke.

00:36:30.043 --> 00:36:32.587
This is really good.
How did you find this place?

00:36:32.670 --> 00:36:34.047
I've got a new go-to now.

00:36:34.672 --> 00:36:36.257
Enjoy your meal, everyone.

00:36:36.341 --> 00:36:38.301
Once Mr. Kim gets back,

00:36:38.384 --> 00:36:40.762
we have to go to
Ttokdari Diner day and night.

00:36:41.930 --> 00:36:43.640
Wait, is it official?

00:36:43.723 --> 00:36:47.936
Normally, the head of HR wouldn't go
to the factory over an accident.

00:36:48.019 --> 00:36:49.521
So something is definitely up.

00:36:50.313 --> 00:36:52.023
-I see.
-Song-hee.

00:36:52.941 --> 00:36:54.609
You need to pick the right side.

00:36:55.360 --> 00:36:56.694
Isn't your profile picture

00:36:56.778 --> 00:36:58.905
the one with your arm around Mr. Do?

00:36:59.531 --> 00:37:01.866
You're right. Shoot, what do I do?

00:37:02.408 --> 00:37:04.202
RECENT PHOTOS

00:37:04.285 --> 00:37:07.330
I'll change it to a group photo
with both of them in it.

00:37:07.413 --> 00:37:10.583
"The leaders I look up to."

00:37:11.084 --> 00:37:12.293
Hearts.

00:37:12.377 --> 00:37:13.753
You're so pathetic.

00:37:13.837 --> 00:37:17.549
Whatever, Song-hee.
You can be as noble as this rock here.

00:37:17.632 --> 00:37:19.592
I'm not ashamed at all.

00:37:28.434 --> 00:37:30.687
LINE 1 PRODUCTION
YOON HYO-SIK

00:37:32.480 --> 00:37:34.899
NO. 21
EVALUATOR: KIM NAK-SU

00:37:39.612 --> 00:37:41.197
SAFETY RULE VIOLATORS

00:37:43.491 --> 00:37:48.162
FINAL LIST OF SAFETY RULE VIOLATORS
VOLUNTARY RETIREMENT CANDIDATES

00:37:58.006 --> 00:37:59.215
What is it?

00:38:01.467 --> 00:38:03.678
If you have nothing to say,
I'm hanging up.

00:38:03.761 --> 00:38:04.679
Okay.

00:38:05.930 --> 00:38:08.308
-You want me to hang up?
-No.

00:38:09.183 --> 00:38:10.184
What's wrong with you?

00:38:11.144 --> 00:38:12.186
What were you doing?

00:38:12.270 --> 00:38:15.231
I have an interview this weekend.

00:38:15.315 --> 00:38:17.692
And I have nothing to wear.

00:38:18.318 --> 00:38:19.736
At a real estate agency?

00:38:20.403 --> 00:38:22.947
-Yes.
-Then buy something to wear.

00:38:24.490 --> 00:38:26.576
Yes, I probably will.

00:38:27.744 --> 00:38:29.913
-You should try to get the job.
-I will.

00:38:32.123 --> 00:38:35.668
What happened?
You said you didn't want me to work.

00:38:36.461 --> 00:38:37.420
I don't know.

00:38:39.547 --> 00:38:40.423
Are you sick?

00:38:41.674 --> 00:38:42.592
No.

00:38:42.675 --> 00:38:43.593
Oh, honey.

00:38:44.594 --> 00:38:48.306
How much do you think you'll get
for your bonus this fall?

00:38:48.806 --> 00:38:49.682
Why do you ask?

00:38:49.766 --> 00:38:53.353
Well, I was thinking we could just pay

00:38:53.436 --> 00:38:56.105
the rest of our mortgage in full.

00:38:56.189 --> 00:38:58.483
What are you talking about?

00:38:58.566 --> 00:39:01.486
You know there's a fee
for paying off a loan early.

00:39:01.569 --> 00:39:05.114
No, it's been over three years,
so the fee is waived.

00:39:05.823 --> 00:39:08.660
We're paying eight million won
a year in interest alone.

00:39:08.743 --> 00:39:10.745
Let's just pay it off. Okay?

00:39:10.828 --> 00:39:13.706
And watching the interest rates
fluctuate stresses me out.

00:39:13.790 --> 00:39:15.708
Let's just let it be. All right?

00:39:15.792 --> 00:39:17.752
You're just listening to nonsense
from somewhere.

00:39:17.835 --> 00:39:20.129
Heard it from whom?

00:39:20.755 --> 00:39:23.174
I'm a licensed real estate agent,
remember?

00:39:24.300 --> 00:39:27.011
Anyway, when that bonus comes in,
don't you dare touch it.

00:39:27.095 --> 00:39:30.098
If we have to, we'll combine it
with next year's Lunar New Year bonus.

00:39:30.181 --> 00:39:31.849
-Got it?
-I'm hanging up.

00:39:31.933 --> 00:39:34.560
Mom sent you
soy-marinated abalone. Did you get--

00:39:48.616 --> 00:39:49.826
Mr. Kim.

00:39:50.827 --> 00:39:52.120
Oh, hi.

00:39:52.203 --> 00:39:53.579
Have you eaten yet?

00:39:53.663 --> 00:39:55.164
-What?
-Of course he hasn't.

00:39:55.248 --> 00:39:56.416
-Let's go inside.
-Where?

00:39:56.499 --> 00:39:57.458
-Come on.
-What?

00:39:57.542 --> 00:39:59.127
-Let's go.
-Inside where?

00:39:59.210 --> 00:40:00.712
This way.

00:40:01.671 --> 00:40:02.672
-Here.
-What?

00:40:02.755 --> 00:40:06.759
Just leave everything soaking in the sink
before you leave, okay?

00:40:06.843 --> 00:40:08.136
-Okay. Bye.
-Thank you.

00:40:08.219 --> 00:40:09.846
-Enjoy your meal.
-Bye now.

00:40:09.929 --> 00:40:11.180
-Bye.
-Yeah.

00:40:11.264 --> 00:40:15.059
All right, everyone. Mr. Kim is here.

00:40:15.143 --> 00:40:16.519
A round of applause!

00:40:22.483 --> 00:40:23.776
-Please take a seat.
-Mr. Kim.

00:40:23.860 --> 00:40:25.653
I feel like I'm crashing the party.

00:40:25.737 --> 00:40:26.946
Not at all. Please sit.

00:40:27.030 --> 00:40:28.698
No, not here.

00:40:29.365 --> 00:40:31.743
You can sit right here.

00:40:32.285 --> 00:40:35.329
I'll just stay for a bit then.

00:40:37.540 --> 00:40:39.167
Mr. Kim. Can I pour you a drink?

00:40:39.250 --> 00:40:41.127
Yes. A glass of soju, please.

00:40:41.878 --> 00:40:43.546
Wait. Hold on a second.

00:40:43.629 --> 00:40:46.007
Pour him a glass of this.

00:40:46.758 --> 00:40:47.884
What's that?

00:40:47.967 --> 00:40:49.427
-Gosh.
-Jeez.

00:40:49.927 --> 00:40:53.347
My wife sent me this.
It's braised tofu. Please try some.

00:40:54.432 --> 00:40:56.976
She makes a mean braised tofu.

00:40:57.602 --> 00:40:59.103
My goodness. Thank you.

00:40:59.187 --> 00:41:00.772
What's going on?

00:41:00.855 --> 00:41:02.482
Why are you giving him
the imported liquor?

00:41:02.565 --> 00:41:04.942
You're drunk. Sit down.

00:41:05.026 --> 00:41:06.944
-Don't take it out on him.
-Think about it.

00:41:07.028 --> 00:41:09.655
What did he do to deserve that?

00:41:09.739 --> 00:41:12.617
He's just itching
to find a reason to fire us.

00:41:12.700 --> 00:41:13.785
Calm down, buddy.

00:41:13.868 --> 00:41:15.995
Behave yourself. Just sit down.

00:41:16.079 --> 00:41:17.872
-Come on.
-I can't lose this job.

00:41:18.706 --> 00:41:21.375
I have two parents at home
who are over 90 years old.

00:41:21.459 --> 00:41:23.628
Hey, that's enough.

00:41:23.711 --> 00:41:26.923
Are you the only one struggling?
Who here doesn't have sick parents?

00:41:27.006 --> 00:41:28.508
Have you saved up any money?

00:41:29.175 --> 00:41:31.844
-I've only saved up debt.
-Sir, shall we have a toast?

00:41:32.512 --> 00:41:34.222
Excuse me, sir.

00:41:34.305 --> 00:41:36.641
Last month, I told you
that the machine was acting up

00:41:36.724 --> 00:41:38.726
and that we needed to stop it.

00:41:38.810 --> 00:41:42.021
Hey, if we were to miss the deadline,
would you take responsibility?

00:41:42.105 --> 00:41:45.775
If someone has to go,
it should be the young guys, right?

00:41:45.858 --> 00:41:47.360
-Us?
-Yes.

00:41:47.443 --> 00:41:52.198
What he means is that young people
have more opportunities, so--

00:41:52.281 --> 00:41:55.326
What kind of opportunities?
Where are they?

00:41:55.409 --> 00:41:58.454
How should I know?
You'd have more than us. Go find them.

00:41:58.538 --> 00:41:59.831
Hey, come on.

00:42:00.373 --> 00:42:03.000
The rule at this factory
is first in, first out.

00:42:03.084 --> 00:42:06.671
It's only fair that you leave
in the order you joined.

00:42:06.754 --> 00:42:08.005
That's harsh.

00:42:08.631 --> 00:42:10.633
So the old-timers should get lost?

00:42:10.716 --> 00:42:11.968
Listen.

00:42:12.051 --> 00:42:14.137
Your movements are just too slow.

00:42:14.220 --> 00:42:17.223
No, everything you do is slow.

00:42:17.306 --> 00:42:20.852
To be blunt,
you guys can't meet your quotas.

00:42:20.935 --> 00:42:23.563
So these young folks right here

00:42:23.646 --> 00:42:26.190
-are all suffering because of you.
-"Suffering"?

00:42:29.193 --> 00:42:31.696
Dal-jae, did you just say "suffering"?

00:42:31.779 --> 00:42:34.907
Are you having trouble hearing?

00:42:36.117 --> 00:42:37.660
-Are you?
-Gosh. Hey.

00:42:37.743 --> 00:42:38.953
"Suffering"!

00:42:39.036 --> 00:42:41.581
-What?
-Hey, you little punks.

00:42:41.664 --> 00:42:45.293
Who do you think taught you the skills
to work in this factory?

00:42:45.376 --> 00:42:46.919
If it weren't for me,

00:42:47.003 --> 00:42:51.048
you'd have lost
a few fingers by now, you punks!

00:42:51.132 --> 00:42:55.011
Gosh, thank you so much
for saving my fingers.

00:42:55.094 --> 00:42:56.804
But it's not like you were born an expert.

00:42:56.888 --> 00:42:59.223
-You learned from the old-timers too!
-You little bastard.

00:42:59.307 --> 00:43:00.266
-Hey, stop.
-What!

00:43:00.349 --> 00:43:02.560
Why are you leaving
all the responsibility to us?

00:43:02.643 --> 00:43:05.980
-Mr. Kim. How old is your kid?
-I'm not leaving it to you.

00:43:06.063 --> 00:43:07.648
-Grab him.
-Come here!

00:43:07.732 --> 00:43:09.984
You damn young punks.

00:43:10.651 --> 00:43:13.321
Hey, that's enough!

00:43:20.661 --> 00:43:23.289
The food's all set out.

00:43:24.207 --> 00:43:27.752
I had the kitchen lady stay late
to make fried eggs and everything.

00:43:27.835 --> 00:43:31.714
So just have some, okay? Please.

00:43:33.841 --> 00:43:35.051
Sit down.

00:43:35.134 --> 00:43:36.594
-Jeez.
-Just sit down.

00:43:36.677 --> 00:43:39.013
-Please sit down.
-Dal-jae, put on your jacket.

00:43:55.238 --> 00:43:56.656
Why don't I…

00:43:58.241 --> 00:44:00.368
make you all a delicious bomb shot?

00:44:03.204 --> 00:44:04.664
Okay, here we go.

00:44:04.747 --> 00:44:10.461
A golden ratio bomb shot I perfected
over 25 years in sales at ACT.

00:44:10.962 --> 00:44:13.297
This isn't your ordinary bomb shot.

00:44:13.381 --> 00:44:16.133
You need to be at the right place
at the right time.

00:44:16.217 --> 00:44:19.053
The hand that makes it matters,
not just the ratio.

00:44:19.136 --> 00:44:20.554
Now prepare to be amazed.

00:44:20.638 --> 00:44:24.433
Okay, here I go!

00:44:25.559 --> 00:44:29.105
The top must overflow
for the bottom to be filled.

00:44:29.188 --> 00:44:31.190
The Trickle-Down Shot.

00:44:35.069 --> 00:44:36.362
Who wants one?

00:44:36.445 --> 00:44:37.321
-Come on.
-Me!

00:44:37.405 --> 00:44:40.324
Great. That'll be 10,000 won, please.

00:44:40.866 --> 00:44:43.536
I'll send you my bank information.

00:44:43.619 --> 00:44:46.539
Here. Pass them along.

00:44:46.622 --> 00:44:48.332
I'll keep them coming.

00:44:49.458 --> 00:44:52.586
We can fight all we want,
but let's have a drink first.

00:44:52.670 --> 00:44:56.257
We're all family here, after all.
So let's look out for each other.

00:44:56.841 --> 00:44:59.051
-Here's to each other!
-Here's to each other!

00:45:06.851 --> 00:45:08.477
Let's go!

00:45:08.561 --> 00:45:10.396
Man, it's cold at night these days.

00:45:11.689 --> 00:45:12.732
It is.

00:45:15.401 --> 00:45:16.902
What did headquarters say?

00:45:17.987 --> 00:45:21.699
Do they want to lay off everyone
from the line where the accident happened?

00:45:24.785 --> 00:45:25.870
Mr. Kim.

00:45:26.787 --> 00:45:29.123
I don't know. I have no idea.

00:45:29.206 --> 00:45:30.207
What if…

00:45:30.291 --> 00:45:32.793
What if I left instead?

00:45:35.880 --> 00:45:36.756
Why you?

00:45:38.799 --> 00:45:40.885
Because I'm the factory supervisor.

00:45:40.968 --> 00:45:44.055
And I'm the team leader.
The Safety Management Team Leader.

00:45:47.641 --> 00:45:48.976
You saw how it is.

00:45:50.603 --> 00:45:53.397
There's not a single person here
who can afford to quit.

00:45:54.482 --> 00:45:56.776
Firing a few of the older guys
won't even make a statement.

00:45:56.859 --> 00:45:58.819
So just as a symbolic gesture,

00:45:59.570 --> 00:46:01.822
let them replace one young supervisor.

00:46:01.906 --> 00:46:03.491
Please take care of it.

00:46:04.909 --> 00:46:06.160
What will you do?

00:46:06.911 --> 00:46:09.205
Me? I have plenty of offers.

00:46:10.456 --> 00:46:12.792
I'm known for being sharp and efficient.

00:46:13.709 --> 00:46:14.627
Gosh.

00:46:17.296 --> 00:46:19.965
I'll take full responsibility.

00:46:20.841 --> 00:46:21.967
Just let me do this.

00:46:25.679 --> 00:46:27.723
Do you have any idea
what you're saying right now?

00:46:27.807 --> 00:46:29.058
Yes, I do.

00:46:30.434 --> 00:46:33.437
If there's one person here
who absolutely cannot be fired,

00:46:33.521 --> 00:46:34.522
it's you.

00:46:35.731 --> 00:46:38.526
You're good at your job.
You're an excellent supervisor.

00:46:38.609 --> 00:46:41.487
Even if this factory
were to shut down completely,

00:46:41.570 --> 00:46:44.240
you should still be working
somewhere in this company.

00:46:44.865 --> 00:46:46.409
That's what I believe.

00:46:46.492 --> 00:46:50.162
Now is not the time for you
to be playing the hero.

00:46:50.246 --> 00:46:52.998
You'll take responsibility for what?
Do you think the company is a joke?

00:46:53.082 --> 00:46:55.084
You think you can boss them around?

00:46:55.167 --> 00:46:56.502
They crunched all the numbers

00:46:56.585 --> 00:46:59.422
and are letting go of people
they don't need anymore.

00:46:59.505 --> 00:47:04.135
That's why… I'm asking for your help.

00:47:04.218 --> 00:47:07.680
I've worked with only numbers
for 25 years.

00:47:07.763 --> 00:47:11.016
And you're asking me to axe you

00:47:11.100 --> 00:47:12.726
just to save those people?

00:47:12.810 --> 00:47:13.978
"Mr. Kim,

00:47:14.812 --> 00:47:17.940
please do a lousy job."
That's what you're asking.

00:47:19.650 --> 00:47:20.526
Jeez.

00:47:21.360 --> 00:47:22.570
I can't do that.

00:47:26.907 --> 00:47:29.493
You're so young and naive.

00:47:31.745 --> 00:47:33.914
Stop talking nonsense.

00:47:35.332 --> 00:47:38.711
And try to hang on to your job
for as long as you can.

00:47:39.920 --> 00:47:41.464
That's what being a parent is.

00:47:42.423 --> 00:47:44.091
Got that, you little know-it-all?

00:47:46.135 --> 00:47:47.636
Stay here until the very end

00:47:48.804 --> 00:47:50.347
and take responsibility.

00:47:51.599 --> 00:47:52.933
That's your job.

00:47:53.809 --> 00:47:55.686
I'm going to go do my job.

00:48:01.484 --> 00:48:02.651
Oh, and…

00:48:03.319 --> 00:48:05.154
I always pay for my booze.

00:48:06.530 --> 00:48:07.406
Here.

00:48:08.991 --> 00:48:09.909
That's too much.

00:48:16.040 --> 00:48:17.208
Man, it's cold.

00:48:40.064 --> 00:48:41.941
BEYOND TELECOMMUNICATION
CONNECTING PEOPLE

00:49:01.293 --> 00:49:03.128
OFFICE OF THE HEAD OF HR

00:49:14.014 --> 00:49:15.808
That's right. Yes.

00:49:15.891 --> 00:49:18.269
Just give me three minutes.

00:49:18.352 --> 00:49:20.229
-I'm sorry. Just a moment.
-Okay.

00:49:22.898 --> 00:49:23.899
Yes.

00:49:25.150 --> 00:49:26.110
Man.

00:49:26.193 --> 00:49:28.153
Speak of the devil.

00:49:28.821 --> 00:49:31.240
He must've been in a hurry.
He arrived early.

00:49:32.157 --> 00:49:35.995
I know, right?
And for something so trivial,

00:49:36.078 --> 00:49:38.497
it took way too long.

00:49:38.581 --> 00:49:41.041
Then instead of doing that,

00:49:41.125 --> 00:49:43.877
how about we have dinner together
after work?

00:49:44.587 --> 00:49:48.632
Mr. Kim is the sales team's star
when it comes to drinking and socializing.

00:49:49.592 --> 00:49:51.093
They say he's very entertaining.

00:49:51.176 --> 00:49:54.680
Okay. I'll call you back later then.
All right.

00:49:57.099 --> 00:49:59.518
Mr. Kim, please come in.

00:50:00.311 --> 00:50:01.270
Have a seat over here.

00:50:08.527 --> 00:50:10.988
How does it feel to be back
at headquarters?

00:50:12.364 --> 00:50:13.991
Well, it's nice.

00:50:14.074 --> 00:50:16.785
You should come back soon.
You've worked so hard.

00:50:16.869 --> 00:50:19.747
And think about
what you'd like to eat later.

00:50:20.831 --> 00:50:22.041
The higher-ups are waiting.

00:50:24.460 --> 00:50:29.131
And about the other day… I was a bit rude.

00:50:29.965 --> 00:50:31.550
Please forgive me, sir.

00:50:32.301 --> 00:50:33.177
I understand.

00:50:35.471 --> 00:50:36.347
Really?

00:50:38.057 --> 00:50:39.058
All right then.

00:50:40.392 --> 00:50:41.518
May I have the list?

00:50:50.402 --> 00:50:52.112
KIM NAK-SU

00:51:01.538 --> 00:51:05.000
Oh, you didn't print it out.
Then can you just send it to me?

00:51:05.626 --> 00:51:08.379
Actually, that's a wireless printer.

00:51:08.462 --> 00:51:10.339
You can print it
directly from your phone.

00:51:10.422 --> 00:51:11.840
SAFETY RULE VIOLATORS LIST

00:51:15.302 --> 00:51:17.346
LINE 1 STAFF: 20 RECOMMENDED
FOR VOLUNTARY RETIREMENT

00:51:19.431 --> 00:51:21.141
Actually, Mr. Kim,
just read them out to me.

00:51:21.225 --> 00:51:22.726
It's only 20 people.

00:51:22.810 --> 00:51:24.103
So, who's number one?

00:51:24.186 --> 00:51:26.271
Let's get this over with
and go eat, shall we?

00:51:26.355 --> 00:51:27.648
All right, who's first?

00:51:30.609 --> 00:51:31.485
NO. 6 LEE DAL-JAE

00:51:31.568 --> 00:51:32.986
NO. 7 SEO JEONG-WON

00:51:42.871 --> 00:51:43.872
I'd like to apply

00:51:45.416 --> 00:51:46.917
for voluntary retirement.

00:51:58.762 --> 00:52:00.681
ACT RETIREMENT APPLICATION

00:52:08.105 --> 00:52:08.981
Here.

00:52:09.064 --> 00:52:12.568
Please write the date you want
your voluntary retirement to take effect.

00:52:12.651 --> 00:52:14.653
Hold on. I'm sorry.

00:52:14.737 --> 00:52:17.489
This is last year's form.
I need to check it.

00:52:19.992 --> 00:52:22.703
No, forget it. Don't worry about the rest.

00:52:22.786 --> 00:52:25.247
Just sign here on the applicant line.

00:52:35.090 --> 00:52:38.969
Mr. Kim, you can just tell me right now.

00:52:39.052 --> 00:52:41.764
So, what date should I put down for you?

00:52:41.847 --> 00:52:43.849
Next week? We can also do tomorrow.

00:52:43.932 --> 00:52:47.686
But wouldn't it be better
to get a few more days' pay?

00:52:48.604 --> 00:52:50.147
You already know the rest, I assume.

00:52:50.230 --> 00:52:53.692
You'll get an additional 200 million won
added to your severance.

00:52:53.776 --> 00:52:55.611
It'll be deposited
to your pension account.

00:52:55.694 --> 00:52:59.615
Unless you need it for something major,
it's best to just leave it there.

00:53:02.659 --> 00:53:03.786
What date should I put?

00:53:05.037 --> 00:53:07.498
-Next week.
-Got it.

00:53:07.581 --> 00:53:11.043
Please sign it so I can submit it
for approval right away.

00:53:11.126 --> 00:53:12.586
APPLICANT: KIM NAK-SU

00:53:18.217 --> 00:53:19.134
Are you done?

00:53:21.053 --> 00:53:22.763
What about unemployment benefits?

00:53:22.846 --> 00:53:24.640
That's not going to be possible.

00:53:24.723 --> 00:53:26.433
Since it's voluntary.

00:53:27.476 --> 00:53:29.770
But it's not like the company
is paying for it.

00:53:32.773 --> 00:53:33.982
Good lord.

00:53:39.488 --> 00:53:44.368
Funny how flexible you become
when it's about you.

00:53:45.452 --> 00:53:47.329
Please, I'm begging you.

00:54:00.217 --> 00:54:01.426
Mr. Kim…

00:54:01.510 --> 00:54:03.220
SUBMIT EMPLOYEE'S RETIREMENT APPLICATION?

00:54:03.303 --> 00:54:04.930
…once you submit, it really is the end.

00:54:05.013 --> 00:54:06.598
A final goodbye.

00:54:07.474 --> 00:54:09.685
There's no turning back after that.

00:54:11.770 --> 00:54:15.899
ACT was your first job, right?

00:54:15.983 --> 00:54:18.902
So you got a job
right after you graduated from college.

00:54:18.986 --> 00:54:20.320
Besides maybe some tutoring,

00:54:20.404 --> 00:54:23.031
you've never had any other job, right?

00:54:23.574 --> 00:54:24.575
Once you click that,

00:54:24.658 --> 00:54:29.454
you're looking at 50 years
of living off your savings.

00:54:30.080 --> 00:54:33.417
It's really over then. No more paychecks.

00:54:33.500 --> 00:54:35.002
From your 330 million won severance,

00:54:35.085 --> 00:54:37.588
how much do you think
will be left after taxes?

00:54:38.130 --> 00:54:40.632
How many years do you think
you can last on that?

00:54:45.470 --> 00:54:46.388
The list.

00:54:47.431 --> 00:54:48.765
Will you give it to me?

00:54:51.393 --> 00:54:52.269
Jeez.

00:54:56.023 --> 00:54:59.276
Mr. Kim, let's get the factory
back to normal quickly,

00:54:59.359 --> 00:55:01.361
and then you can return to headquarters

00:55:01.445 --> 00:55:04.281
to really show your potential
and become an executive.

00:55:04.364 --> 00:55:08.493
So our company can focus its resources
and move on to the next step.

00:55:08.994 --> 00:55:10.662
This list of yours

00:55:10.746 --> 00:55:14.750
is the crucial first step
in that whole process.

00:55:17.628 --> 00:55:20.047
Come on, say something. What should we do?

00:55:20.130 --> 00:55:23.300
I'm… doing this because I'm desperate.

00:55:23.383 --> 00:55:26.386
This is the first time
I've ever gone this far. Okay?

00:55:26.470 --> 00:55:28.513
Mr. Kim. Sir!

00:55:29.056 --> 00:55:30.766
Say something!

00:55:36.980 --> 00:55:38.565
God, you talk a lot.

00:55:42.444 --> 00:55:44.237
SUBMIT EMPLOYEE'S RETIREMENT APPLICATION?

00:55:44.905 --> 00:55:46.740
KIM NAK-SU
PERIOD OF EMPLOYMENT: 25 YEARS

00:55:46.823 --> 00:55:48.700
SUBMITTED

00:55:50.827 --> 00:55:52.079
RETIREMENT APPLICATION SUBMITTED

00:55:52.162 --> 00:55:53.455
THIS IS MANAGEMENT SUPPORT

00:56:11.473 --> 00:56:14.518
GENERAL MANAGER KIM NAK-SU

00:56:30.826 --> 00:56:32.500
GENERAL MANAGER DO JIN-WOO

00:56:36.748 --> 00:56:38.208
JUNG SUNG-GU

00:56:47.907 --> 00:56:49.428
AWARD PRESENTED TO
KIM NAK-SU

00:57:00.856 --> 00:57:02.566
We exceeded our targets…

00:57:06.445 --> 00:57:09.156
It boosted sales of our main product…

00:57:13.660 --> 00:57:15.162
…17.9%…

00:57:18.999 --> 00:57:20.208
-Mr. Baek.
-Yes.

00:57:21.293 --> 00:57:23.128
Sorry. Go on.

00:57:23.211 --> 00:57:24.671
I'll continue.

00:57:24.755 --> 00:57:26.882
You'll notice a 12% growth
in the second quarter

00:57:26.965 --> 00:57:28.550
compared to the first quarter.

00:57:28.633 --> 00:57:29.676
CHOI JAE-HYEOK, HEAD OF HR

00:57:29.760 --> 00:57:32.054
KIM NAK-SU APPLIED
FOR VOLUNTARY RETIREMENT AND LEFT

00:57:32.137 --> 00:57:34.347
Especially new contracts
with small companies…

00:57:50.739 --> 00:57:52.324
ADD A WAYPOINT

00:57:52.407 --> 00:57:53.700
THE ROUTE HAS BEEN SET

00:57:53.784 --> 00:57:56.620
MY HOME

00:57:57.829 --> 00:57:59.206
Gosh, I'm exhausted.

00:57:59.289 --> 00:58:01.041
-Song-hee.
-Yes?

00:58:01.124 --> 00:58:04.628
A one-million-won raise versus
leaving at 4 p.m. What would you choose?

00:58:07.005 --> 00:58:09.007
I'd have to seriously think about that.

00:58:09.091 --> 00:58:10.675
I'd definitely choose leaving at 4 p.m.

00:58:10.759 --> 00:58:12.511
Time is going so damn slow.

00:58:19.309 --> 00:58:20.185
Did someone come by?

00:58:20.268 --> 00:58:21.937
Who would come here?

00:58:22.604 --> 00:58:25.023
No, seriously. It's…

00:58:26.399 --> 00:58:28.151
The air feels different, you know?

00:58:29.319 --> 00:58:33.281
I know you don't want to work,
but blaming the air is a new one.

00:58:33.365 --> 00:58:35.242
No, for real. What is it?

00:58:53.051 --> 00:58:53.927
No way.

00:59:02.727 --> 00:59:03.770
Goodness.

00:59:04.855 --> 00:59:06.439
What? What is it?

00:59:32.757 --> 00:59:34.050
I'm home.

00:59:43.101 --> 00:59:44.311
What's going on?

00:59:44.394 --> 00:59:45.645
Is there anything to eat?

00:59:47.147 --> 00:59:48.398
Well, yes.

00:59:49.191 --> 00:59:50.233
Just give me anything.

00:59:50.317 --> 00:59:52.527
Okay. I will.

01:00:04.289 --> 01:00:06.583
Did you take a half-day or something?

01:00:12.964 --> 01:00:14.216
Oh, right.

01:00:22.057 --> 01:00:22.974
Look.

01:00:24.768 --> 01:00:25.685
What?

01:00:25.769 --> 01:00:27.604
I told you.
I have an interview this weekend.

01:00:28.521 --> 01:00:30.398
-For the real estate agency?
-Yes.

01:00:32.651 --> 01:00:33.735
The left one.

01:00:33.818 --> 01:00:34.819
This one?

01:00:36.947 --> 01:00:39.699
-I think this one is better.
-Why ask if you won't listen?

01:00:39.783 --> 01:00:44.204
I went to the department store
with Ha-yeong and bought this today.

01:00:44.287 --> 01:00:45.747
Jeez, you know what?

01:00:45.830 --> 01:00:47.415
She said she'd buy it for me,

01:00:47.499 --> 01:00:50.794
but the moment she saw the price tag,
she completely changed her tune.

01:00:50.877 --> 01:00:54.714
She forgot how I worked
my fingers to the bone

01:00:54.798 --> 01:00:58.802
to pay for her tuition.
Honestly, what a little brat.

01:00:58.885 --> 01:01:01.680
I should've taken that car back then.

01:01:01.763 --> 01:01:02.847
Right?

01:01:06.685 --> 01:01:08.019
Am I right or not?

01:01:09.187 --> 01:01:10.272
You're right.

01:01:50.228 --> 01:01:51.438
What was that for?

01:01:56.234 --> 01:01:57.319
What's with you?

01:02:01.573 --> 01:02:03.992
Hey, stop it.

01:02:06.786 --> 01:02:08.246
-Hey!
-Cut it out.

01:02:08.330 --> 01:02:09.497
Hey, Mr. Unemployed.

01:02:09.581 --> 01:02:12.417
-Hey there, unemployed Mr. Kim.
-Seriously, stop it.

01:02:13.460 --> 01:02:16.171
Your wife has a job interview
this weekend.

01:02:16.254 --> 01:02:17.589
Are you just going to sit around?

01:02:17.672 --> 01:02:19.507
-Give me a break.
-Huh? Come on.

01:02:20.759 --> 01:02:22.552
How much is your severance?

01:02:22.635 --> 01:02:23.595
-Stop it.
-Hand it over.

01:02:23.678 --> 01:02:25.472
Give it to me.

01:02:25.972 --> 01:02:27.766
I'll go buy a new bag and some clothes.

01:02:27.849 --> 01:02:30.310
-And go on a trip abroad.
-You're unbelievable.

01:02:30.393 --> 01:02:32.896
-Come on.
-Just get me something to eat.

01:02:32.979 --> 01:02:34.898
Give me the money. Money, money.

01:02:34.981 --> 01:02:36.358
If you give me a million won,

01:02:36.441 --> 01:02:38.318
-I'll make you the best ramyeon ever.
-Good lord.

01:02:38.401 --> 01:02:40.111
Come on. I told you to stop.

01:02:56.503 --> 01:02:57.879
You've been through so much.

01:02:58.922 --> 01:02:59.798
General Manager Kim.

01:03:07.347 --> 01:03:08.348
I'm sorry.

01:03:12.769 --> 01:03:14.938
What are you sorry for?

01:03:54.727 --> 01:03:56.688
Oh, honey.

01:04:12.201 --> 01:04:17.167
THE DREAM LIFE OF MR. KIM

01:04:47.363 --> 01:04:49.240
You're cut out for the corporate life.

01:04:49.324 --> 01:04:51.951
Don't even think about doing
what you're planning right now.

01:04:52.035 --> 01:04:53.786
So what will you be doing now?

01:04:53.870 --> 01:04:55.830
I bet the severance pay wasn't much.

01:04:55.914 --> 01:04:58.541
Team 1 doesn't need to attend,
so I didn't tell you.

01:04:58.625 --> 01:05:01.920
He's letting us know
we're just Kim Nak-su's guys.

01:05:02.003 --> 01:05:04.422
I can't go higher than two million.

01:05:04.506 --> 01:05:06.508
Until last week, I was a general manager.

01:05:06.591 --> 01:05:08.551
I can't work for that kind of money.

01:05:08.635 --> 01:05:09.511
SOL E&T CEO CHO YUN-HYEONG

01:05:09.594 --> 01:05:11.679
Is this the business
you wanted us to start?

01:05:12.847 --> 01:05:13.723
DAHAN REAL ESTATE

01:05:13.806 --> 01:05:14.766
-Hello.
-Jeez.

01:05:14.849 --> 01:05:18.603
This location is one of the best
I've seen in my entire career.

01:05:18.686 --> 01:05:20.855
This electrifying tension.

01:05:20.939 --> 01:05:22.982
This gambler's instinct.

01:05:26.947 --> 01:05:28.947
Subtitle translation by Soya Back